    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the value is returned as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated DTOs accept it on input and expose it on output (the `Owner` response schema inherits it via `allOf`). MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the body omitted it (a supplied date is preserved).\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n- **Seed data** (`hsqldb`, `mysql` positional `data.sql` inserts) \u2014 added the extra `NULL` value so the column count matches; `h2`/`postgres` use named-column inserts and needed no change.\n\nJackson serializes `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` by default, satisfying both the \"defaults to today\" and \"keeps supplied date\" test cases. The full suite (14 tests) is green.",
